# ── RAG data (runtime, not source) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# DATA_ROOT is anchored to the PACKAGE now — config.py derives _BACKEND_ROOT from
# __file__ — so the live stores land in Backend/data/ no matter where the server
# is started from. Backend/src/data/ is kept as a belt-and-braces entry: a relative
# DATA_ROOT set in .env IS still resolved against the working directory, which is
# how the stores ended up under src/ before the anchoring landed.
Backend/src/data/
Backend/data/

# ── Node / Frontend ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
Frontend/dist/

# The design lab is throwaway scratch — candidates, rejected directions, the
# gallery shell. It holds NO live data and may be deleted at any time; nothing
# reads it, and the build must never require it. The live design system is
# Frontend/src/assets/main.css, which is committed like any other source file.
Frontend/design/theme-lab/
Frontend/.env
Frontend/.env.local
Frontend/.env.*.local

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

